    "narrative": "Our strongest offensive engine today is centered in the favorable hitting environment against Tomoyuki Sugano, making **Kyle Tucker** (85.90) and **Andy Pages** (74.42) the pillars of the lineup. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from an elite combination of a high base projection and a massive +14% park adjustment, while **Andy Pages** leverages the same park factor alongside a favorable matchup against the right-handed Sugano. Similarly, **Drake Baldwin** (71.82) is a mandatory start; despite the \"Lineup Pending\" status, his elite matchup against Ober (4.81 xERA) and the benefit of a +5% wind-out factor significantly boost his daily outlook, making him our highest-projected catcher. **Dominic Smith** (61.88) rounds out the strong tier, with the same weather-driven wind advantage helping him overcome a bottom-third batting order position.\n\nOur most difficult decision involved balancing high-floor bats against the scarcity of stolen bases. **Jackson Merrill** (53.97) ultimately edged out the rest of the bench to take the UTIL slot, as his favorable platoon split against McLean (R) narrowly outweighed the marginal projections of **Coby Mayo** (47.65) and **Sam Antonacci** (48.29). **Sam Antonacci** and **Gunnar Henderson** faced the heaviest resistance today due to the \"left-on-left\" penalty against Shota Imanaga and McClanahan, respectively, though both are kept in the lineup given the lack of superior active alternatives. We remain cautious regarding **Luis Robert Jr.** (52.59); while his physical tools are elite, the -15% dynamic platoon penalty against Buehler limits his ceiling, necessitating a close watch on his final lineup confirmation. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Heliot Ramos** unavailable due to injury or scheduling, the roster depth is stretched; we are prepared to pivot to high-upside bench options like **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, or **Luis Lara** should any late-scratch announcements emerge from the pending lineups.",
